  "internal_command_rule":"Accepted SR/RFC source projection and import-driven SR reference reconciliation are invoked only by LLD-04 inside its shared UnitOfWork and have no public import-bypass route.",
  "route_rules":[
    "All routes require LLD-12 authenticated loopback browser context; mutations additionally require anti-forgery and COMMAND_ENVELOPE_V1.",
    "RFC terminal-cascade execution additionally requires the session-bound deliberate_action_proof contained in ExecuteRfcTerminalCascadeRequestV1 and bound to exact proposal revision plus scope fingerprint.",
    "DELETE on SR reference/relationship/note routes means governed supersede/unlink/remove command, never master Customer/Contact deletion or generic record destruction.",
    "reference_role is a closed enum customer_contact|current_handler_reference and never becomes dynamic SQL.",
    "Current Handler Contact routes cannot create local handler authority; they only resolve an exact current accepted source observation.",
    "RFC hard deletion is exposed only through explicit hard-delete preview/action routes and never through a generic DELETE /rfcs/{id} endpoint.",
    "Archive restoration targets immutable archive-operation identity rather than a mutable current branch selection.",
    "Terminal-cascade preview/refresh/execute are distinct operations; preview and refresh never execute downstream consequences.",
    "ticket_type is a closed enum resolved to static owner code and is never concatenated into SQL/table names.",
    "Subordinate-origin SR proposals target the governing root; the client cannot force a subordinate direct SR link.",
    "Device Reference link routes always target device_reference_id and never accept network_element_id as replacement operational identity."
  ]
}
